    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "WANG Shih-to 汪士鐸 (original ming 鏊, T. 振庵, 晉侯, 梅村 H. 悔翁, 芝生, 無不悔翁}}, July 14, 1802–1889, Aug. 3, scholar, was a native of Nanking. His father, Wang Chün 汪均 (T. 治平, 1765–1832), was a follower of Neo-Confucianism and a strict disciplinarian.",
